  "cfSelect_noticeTitle": "How the new version connects to linux.do",
  "cfSelect_noticeBody": "Starting with this version, CFluxDo finds Cloudflare nodes that can reach linux.do on its own and no longer relies on any relay service by default:\n• It sends a small number of domain queries to public DNS services such as Tencent DNSPod, Alibaba AliDNS, 360, Cloudflare, Google and Quad9 (for Cloudflare-hosted sites of large companies such as Visa, OpenAI and Shopify, plus the node list at atlas.1molchuan.top) to obtain candidate nodes and encryption keys. Queries contain only domain names, never any of your account information.\n• It performs encrypted handshakes (ECH) with several Cloudflare nodes and requests /cdn-cgi/trace to measure speed, then remembers the best one; it re-measures only when the network changes or the connection fails.\n• A single measurement uses roughly 50–200 KB of data.\nThe current route is shown at the top of App Settings → Network; you can switch to “atlas pool only” under Advanced settings → Node selection.\n\nHelp selection (off by default): when enabled, the app shares the measurements it already makes with the community node site cfhub, helping other users on the same carrier find nodes faster. Enabling it requires authorizing cfhub via Connect with your linux.do account (the same as joining on the cfhub website; trust level 1 or above required). We promise:\n• Only candidate Cloudflare node addresses, handshake latency and success/failure are shared; nothing shared contains cookies, tokens, device identifiers or browsing history.\n• cfhub records your linux.do username and trust level, plus the carrier and region this share belongs to; it does not store your full IP address.\n• No extra measurements run in the background, so no extra battery or data use; if a share fails it is dropped, never retried.\n• You can turn it off in Settings at any time; turning it off takes effect immediately and invalidates the authorization. Logging out of linux.do also invalidates it.\n• Both the client code and the sharing format are open source.",
  "cfSelect_noticeKeepOff": "Keep off",
  "cfSelect_noticeEnable": "Enable and help selection",
